@Mix1mum In communism, we are all poor and stay poor. In capitalism, the rich get richer quicker, but the poor also get richer, even tho slower.
The default state of every living being is the poverty. If your parent give you something, it's their will. Whether it's money or social capital.
In my country, people forget what they had(n't) before the fall of the regime.

@zpardus "Ability?"

The Astors made their money peddling Opium to China. They were the billionaires of their era.

The Roosevelts made their money the old fashioned way - they inherited land grants from a royal charter, on land expropriated from the natives (I hear Americans are "very concerned" about "genocide in Gaza" these days. Too bad they weren't so "concerned" when the victims were at the end of their own gun barrels.)

@PedestrianPony  Also America doesn’t even have a housing bubble.

The Sydney metro area has the same home prices as New York City, with the median household income of Idaho and Georgia.

In China that math gets even more ridiculous so I have to chuckle when people here complain about sunbelt mini mansions being 800k, it can be A LOT worse.
